  "articleBody": "Upgrading your garage interior often starts with deciding how to finish the walls and slab. Weighing taped drywall against bare framing, and finished flooring against raw concrete, determines your space's comfort and function.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options\n- Bare Framing vs. Finished Drywall: Exposed studs leave wiring vulnerable, collect cobwebs, and allow drafts. Hanging and taping drywall provides clean, bright surfaces, improves fire resistance between garage and home, and creates a finished backdrop for hanging tool tracks and cabinets.\n- Bare Concrete vs. Moisture-Resistant Floor Finishes: Untreated concrete absorbs automotive fluids, generates dust, and shows every freeze-thaw stain. High-grade coatings or specialized slab sealers resist chemical spills, wash clean easily, and prevent oils from soaking into porous masonry.\n- Workshop Comfort vs. Basic Vehicle Parking: If the garage serves strictly as parking, standard drywall and concrete sealing may suffice. If you plan a hobby shop, gym, or heated workspace, pair insulated drywall assemblies with sealed floors to hold warmth and reduce dust.\n\nHH Remodeling LLC provides custom drywall installation, framing, and interior finish carpentry across Denver and Aurora. Call 303-505-0866 today to review your garage upgrade options with owner Abraham Becerra.",
